utor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also coherent: it records the healthy held package before restart, schedules the reboot, observes temporary SSH unavailability, proves a different boot identity, and verifies recovered curl functionality, package state, OS release, and kernel. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The apt simulations reported no available package upgrades and curl's candidate already equaled its installed version, so the hold was not exercised against a genuinely newer curl candidate.","Systemd failed-service inspection was unsupported on this legacy platform; other captured recovery and package-health evidence was healthy."]}
